### Ví dụ 3: Cost Optimization Review

```typescript
// Review vector search costs
async function reviewVectorSearchCosts(
  impl: VectorSearchImplementation,
  usageMetrics: UsageMetrics
): Promise<CostOptimizationReport> {
  const currentCosts = calculateCurrentCosts(impl, usageMetrics);
  
  const optimizations: CostOptimization[] = [];
  
  // Quantize vectors
  if (impl.vector_dimensions > 768) {
    const quantized = await estimateQuantization(impl, 'pq', 128);
    optimizations.push({
      type: 'quantization',
      description: 'PQ quantization to 128 bytes',
      cost_reduction: quantized.savings_usd,
      recall_impact: -quantized.recall_loss
    });
  }
  
  // Reduce index precision
  if (impl.metric === 'euclidean') {
    const float16 = await estimateFloat16(impl);
    optimizations.push({
      type: 'precision_reduction',
      description: 'Use float16 instead of float32',
      cost_reduction: float16.savings_usd,
      recall_impact: -float16.recall_loss
    });
  }
  
  // Batch queries
  const batchSavings = await estimateBatchProcessing(impl, usageMetrics);
  optimizations.push({
    type: 'batch_processing',
    description: 'Enable query batching',
    cost_reduction: batchSavings.usd,
    recall_impact: 0
  });
  
  return {
    current_monthly_cost: currentCosts,
    optimizations: optimizations.sort((a, b) => b.cost_reduction - a.cost_reduction),
    total_potential_savings: sum(optimizations.map(o => o.cost_reduction)),
    recommendations: generateCostRecommendations(optimizations)
  };
}
```

## Anti Patterns (Các pattern cần tránh)

### 1. One-Size-Fits-All Index
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Same index config for all use cases
const index = await pinecone.createIndex({
  metric: 'cosine',
  index_type: 'hnsw'
});

// ✅ GOOD: Workload-specific configurations
const configs = {
  'high-recall': { m: 32, ef_construction: 400 },
  'low-latency': { m: 16, ef_construction: 200 },
  'memory-constrained': { m: 8, ef_construction: 100 }
};
```

### 2. Ignoring Query Patterns
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Same top_k for all queries
async function badSearch(query) {
  return await index.search(query, { top_k: 100 });
}

// ✅ GOOD: Query-aware top_k
async function goodSearch(query: SearchQuery) {
  const topK = getOptimalTopK(query.type);
  return await index.search(query, { top_k: topK });
}
```

### 3. No Performance Monitoring
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Deploy and forget
async function badDeploy(index) {
  await index.create();
  return index;
}

// ✅ GOOD: Full observability
async function goodDeploy(index) {
  await index.create();
  await setupMonitoring(index, {
    latency: true,
    quality: true,
    resource_usage: true,
    cost_tracking: true
  });
  return index;
}
```

### 4. Skipping Quality Validation
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Trust vector search implicitly
const results = await search(query);
return results;

// ✅ GOOD: Validate and monitor quality
const results = await search(query);
const quality = await validateResults(query, results);
if (quality.recall < THRESHOLD) {
  await alert('Low recall detected');
}
return results;
```

### 5. Manual Parameter Tuning
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Manual guess-based tuning
const params = { m: 16, ef_search: 50 }; // Arbitrary values

// ✅ GOOD: Systematic parameter optimization
const params = await optimizeParameters(impl, {
  search_space: { m: [8, 16, 32], ef_search: [50, 100, 200] },
  objective: 'maximize recall_at_10 with p95_latency < 50ms',
  constraints: { memory_gb: 32 }
});
```

## Best Practices (Thực hành tốt nhất)

1. **Profile before optimizing**: Know your baseline trước khi thay đổi
2. **Quality first, then speed**: Recall > Latency
3. **Use benchmarks with ground truth**: Generic benchmarks may not reflect your use case
4. **Monitor continuously**: Performance can degrade over time
5. **Plan for scale**: Design for 10x current volume
6. **Document all configurations**: Including rationale
7. **Test in staging**: Never tune directly in production
8. **Have rollback plan**: Every change should be reversible
9. **Track costs**: Vector search can get expensive
10. **Automate optimization**: Use systematic tuning tools

